      "administering_agency": "City of Burlingame Community Development Department, Planning Division",
      "funding_type": "regulatory requirement",
      "typical_award_size": "Fee-based program adopted after a legal challenge to the former inclusionary ordinance (Ordinance 2000 of 2021, amended by Ordinance 2046 on March 2, 2026). Residential impact fee on residential floor area for rental projects over 10 units and for-sale projects over 6 units, with rates in the Master Fee Schedule (not opened this pass); on-site alternative deems impacts mitigated with 10% low income plus 5% very low income rental units in perpetuity or 15% low income for-sale units for 55 years. Commercial linkage fee on hotel, retail, restaurant, service and office projects adding 5,000 square feet or more, with rates in the Master Fee Schedule; the first four years produced more than $3.8 million. Both feed the Affordable Housing Fund.",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not applicable.",
